# SmartVision AI: Intelligent Multi-Class Object Recognition System

## 1. Project Overview

SmartVision AI is a deep learning-based computer vision system designed to perform image classification and object detection. The project combines transfer learning models for classification and YOLOv8 for object detection to recognize multiple object categories from images.

The system supports 25 selected object classes derived from the COCO dataset and provides an interactive web application built using Streamlit. Users can upload images, classify objects, detect multiple objects within images, and view model performance metrics.

---

## 2. Problem Statement

Object recognition is one of the most important tasks in computer vision. Traditional image processing techniques often fail to generalize across different environments and object variations.

The objective of this project is to develop an intelligent system capable of:

* Classifying images into predefined categories.
* Detecting and localizing objects within images.
* Comparing multiple deep learning architectures.
* Deploying an interactive web application for end users.

---

## 3. Dataset Description

The dataset was created using selected categories from the COCO (Common Objects in Context) dataset.

### Selected Classes

* Airplane
* Bed
* Bench
* Bicycle
* Bird
* Bottle
* Bowl
* Bus
* Cake
* Car
* Cat
* Chair
* Couch
* Cow
* Cup
* Dog
* Elephant
* Horse
* Motorcycle
* Person
* Pizza
* Potted Plant
* Stop Sign
* Traffic Light
* Truck

### Dataset Statistics

#### Classification Dataset

* Training Images: 1750
* Validation Images: 375
* Test Images: 375
* Total Images: 2500

#### Detection Dataset

* Images: 2125
* Labels: 2125
* Objects: 21578

---

## 4. Dataset Preparation

The dataset preparation pipeline was automated using Python and Jupyter Notebook.

The following steps were performed:

1. COCO annotations loading
2. Category filtering
3. Image extraction
4. Image resizing
5. Dataset splitting
6. YOLO annotation generation
7. Label validation and cleaning

The final dataset was organized into:

### Classification Structure

classification/
├── train/
├── val/
└── test/

### Detection Structure

detection/
├── images/
└── labels/

---

## 5. Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)

EDA was performed to understand dataset characteristics.

### Key Findings

* Dataset contains 25 object categories.
* Class distribution is balanced.
* Images are evenly distributed across train, validation, and test sets.
* Detection dataset contains more than 21,000 object annotations.
* Average objects per image: approximately 10.

Visualization techniques included:

* Class distribution charts
* Image count analysis
* Dataset summary statistics

---

## 6. Image Classification Models

Transfer learning was used to leverage pretrained CNN architectures.

### MobileNetV2

MobileNetV2 is a lightweight CNN architecture optimized for efficiency and deployment on resource-constrained devices.

Validation Accuracy: 40.27%

### VGG16

VGG16 is a deep convolutional neural network consisting of 16 layers.

Validation Accuracy: 15.73%

### ResNet50

ResNet50 utilizes residual connections to enable deeper network training.

Validation Accuracy: 8.80%

### EfficientNetB0

EfficientNetB0 scales network depth, width, and resolution efficiently.

Validation Accuracy: 4.00%

### Best Performing Classification Model

MobileNetV2 achieved the highest validation accuracy and was selected for deployment.

---

## 7. Object Detection Using YOLOv8

YOLOv8 was used for real-time object detection.

### Training Configuration

* Model: YOLOv8n
* Input Size: 640 × 640
* Dataset: Custom COCO subset
* Framework: Ultralytics YOLO

### Evaluation Metrics

Precision: 0.453

Recall: 0.429

mAP50: 0.385

mAP50-95: 0.162

YOLO successfully detected multiple object categories and generated bounding boxes around identified objects.

---

## 8. Model Evaluation

### Classification Comparison

| Model          | Validation Accuracy |
| -------------- | ------------------- |
| MobileNetV2    | 40.27%              |
| VGG16          | 15.73%              |
| ResNet50       | 8.80%               |
| EfficientNetB0 | 4.00%               |

### Detection Performance

| Metric    | Value |
| --------- | ----- |
| Precision | 0.453 |
| Recall    | 0.429 |
| mAP50     | 0.385 |
| mAP50-95  | 0.162 |

MobileNetV2 outperformed the other classification models, while YOLOv8 provided acceptable object detection performance.

